Chrome is the fourth studio album by American country music singer Trace Adkins. It was released on October 9, 2001, on Capitol Records Nashville. The album produced three singles for Adkins on the "Billboard" Hot Country Songs charts: "I'm Tryin'" at No. 6, "Help Me Understand" at No. 17, and the title track at No. 10. It has also been certified gold by the RIAA. The album was produced by Trey Bruce (tracks 3, 5–8, 10, 11) and Dann Huff (tracks 1, 2, 4, 9, 12). The album's title track was later covered by Jeffrey Steele on his 2003 album "Gold, Platinum, Chrome, and Steele". Personnel. Adapted from "Chrome" liner notes. Technical. All tracks mastered by Glenn Meadows
